KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
must never appear
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/11: an unused non-virtual member function shall not be
implicitly instantiated.  CBMC currently instantiates unused member bodies
eagerly (instantiate_template's deferred-method loop), so unused()'s assertion
"must never appear" enters the goto program (vacuously SUCCESS).  The forbidden
pattern therefore matches today, so this test passes as KNOWNBUG.

Under Option B (on-odr-use instantiation) unused() is never instantiated and
the message disappears; the test then succeeds and should be reclassified to
CORE.  Precise lazy-vs-eager discriminator.  See
doc/architectural/cpp-extern-template-member-instantiation.md.
